Okay... I'm kinda upset as I write this... I've been working on this
character for well over a month, went genoless, wishless, and
polyless, and it's been so long since I last ascended I was hoping
very much for a chance. Instead everything turns out for the worst and
I had a very rough time while going through the planes. I'll start
there, and if you want to hear how the rest of the game went just
ask...

*quickie summary*
Got a pet winged gargoyle early on from a wand of poly, who helped
lots but killed too many shopkeepers, and killed an aligned priest
when I was literally going to burdened just from all the gold I was
carrying, and wouldn't go away even when magic missiled.

Some luck with bones early on, getting four magic markers and a silver
dragon scale mail. I didn't feel very confident though since the last
five characters to get the same dragon scale mail all died unusual
deaths (This one too I guess *sigh*)

Everything else went smoothly, and I was totally shocked to be able to
go wishless, I was determined to ascend this time around,
unfortunantly this turned out to be a cruel taunt and I wasn't very
happy about it. I died ~3~ times, which is stark raving crazy.
Survived the entire game right until hitting the astral plain. AC at
-50 (from protection) and I still got hurt like crazy.

Now, earth went okay, and I didn't have any issues with it. And Water
and Fire were easy and a peace of cake. (Aside from the wizard showing
up on water). The problem was Air, the Elementals were voracious! I
lost all the charges on my wand of death to them, after using up all
except 1 potion of full healing. Now... I know you can teleport them
away, and avoid them etc... but this time around I'd escape an
elemental, get swallowed again, escape again, then get swallowed
again, take a step, get swallowed again, you get the idea. Even with
free action I'd get frozen in the clouds, I've never had so much
trouble before, I could hardly move a single square!

After ~finally~ escaping the plane of air and trudging through water
to astral, the trouble began.

Now... I went for the closest altar, but 2 arch-liches immidiately
teleported next to me and started summoning storms. I'd dealt with
this before so it wasn't so bad. As I moved along (not even all the
way up the very first hallway towards the closest altar) Pestilence
came along, I zapped the final charge on my remaining wand of death
(my magic markers all dried out just before heading off, I thought 7
charges would be enough *sigh* I hate air elementals more than ever)
It missed, I teled pestilence off, tried to take a step, and
immidiately got surrounded by green slimes and a couple mindflayers. I
quickly engraved elbereth and tried to gradually move towards the
door, but a Minotaur was in the way. After killing off the mindflayers
and the minotaur, and the slimes I took another step. I got one of the
archliches too, pesitilence showed up and I teled it off again, trying
to deal with the liches. But with a priest of Moloch, a couple
minotaurs, and a mind flayer trying to suck at my brains, I died for
the first time. I survived, got engulfed by pestilence a turn later,
and immidiately died again. Fought off some more mind flayers and
another minotaur, and died by pestilence after losing my potions
almost... maybe I should of quaffed it, I hardly even got enough
time... *sigh*

I wouldn't have made it out of that storm... it was packed solid with
minotaurs and ettins, and with pestilence and priests of moloch it was
a hopeless cause. The best way to handle storms like that is to just
avoid them entirely, I learned that lesson early on... A way to handle
it would have been to break genoless conduct and get rid of the
liches, but I didn't expect to have such horrid luck with them. I
mean, I'd survived worse already in this game, and dealt with four of
them at a time, it was dumb luck to keep getting mindflayers with
every summon, along with minotaurs which ignore elbereth.....

And please don't say I could have avoided it if I quaffed the potion
of full healing, I would have just died again in a few more turns (all
the deaths were close together and I was trying everything I could)
and genoing the liches wasn't an option, this is a conduct game.




